## 1. The diff

Above is the exact diff for `test/README.md`, the three `yang` tests, `module_test.cljc`, and `v2_test.cljc`. `test/yin/vm/parity_test.cljc` was rewritten per D4 (key hunks: corpus rows are now `[name ast expected]`; the four deftests compare v2 against the pinned column; v1/`dao.stream` requires and `run-v1` deleted; docstring states the column and capture date 2026-09-16).

One deviation worth naming: `clojure_test.clj`'s helpers merge `:modules (module/register-stream-module (module/default-registry))` into the base VM opts. Without it the three `test-stream-end-to-end` cases failed — v1 registered the `stream` module globally at load time, and v2's composition must register it explicitly (same wiring as `yin.repl.core:273`). Assertions in those tests are unchanged.

## 2. Captured parity values and how

Capture ran against v1 still in the tree, via a temporary scratch namespace (now deleted) that called the parity test's own `run-v1` on each corpus row — `clj -M:test -n scratch.capture-test`, i.e. the exact `run-v1` code path, JVM. Run twice; values identical (the two nondeterministic-looking rows are per-fresh-VM counters, deterministic: `:p-0`, `:stream-0`).

| case | v1 captured |
|---|---|
| literal int/string/nil/vector/map/set | `42`, `"hello world"`, `nil`, `[1 2 3]`, `{:x 10, :y 20}`, `#{1 2}` |
| add/sub/mul/div | `30`, `5`, `50`, `4` |
| =/= t/</> | `true`, `false`, `true`, `true` |
| nested application, if t/f, lambda app | `6`, `100`, `200`, `11` |
| closure value | `{:type :closure, :params ['x], :body {:type :variable, :name 'x}}` |
